WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.750
Luke Skywalker has pretty much always been
at the center of the Star Wars stories.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.480
He was the hero whose journey the entire original
trilogy centered on.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.200
His birth was the endgame of the prequels.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.980
And the new film series seems to focus first
on finding him, and then building his relationship

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:16.740
with Rey.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.440
But in footage for The Last Jedi, he looks
much more troubled than usual.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.640
So, what does it mean that Luke's demeanor
seems so much darker than what we've seen

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.180
in the past?

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.640
Let's explore some of the possible consequences
for Luke's new outlook...

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.720
Who's the last Jedi?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.879
Writer-director Rian Johnson said point-blank
on Twitter that Luke is the "last Jedi" mentioned

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.340
in the title to Episode VIII.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.380
But filmmakers lie to their audiences all
the time, so until the movie hits theaters,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.720
it's fair game to speculate.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.480
If Luke has begun to journey down a path of
darkness, he'd no longer be a Jedi and the

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.420
Order would be done.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.570
But perhaps what Johnson meant is not that
Luke is the last Jedi ever, but that he's

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.160
the last of the Jedi as we've come to know
them throughout the franchise.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:05.060
The Jedi we've seen so far in the Star Wars
movies have been plagued by politics and war

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.390
and have strayed from the Jedi Code while
claiming to follow it.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.720
Their arrogance and blindness led to their
virtual decimation.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:15.890
And even Luke's path to becoming a Jedi in
the original trilogy didn't seem to introduce

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.760
a true new Jedi Order.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.680
So, if by Episode VIII, Luke is turning away
from the teachings of the Jedi himself, then

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.870
the Jedi as we've come to know them could
be over, leaving Luke as the last Jedi of

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:29.380
his kind.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.750
The question is this: will the decline of
that particular type of Jedi happen while

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.900
a new and improved Order is formed by, say,
Rey?

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.300
It's a nice idea at the very least.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.340
Is it even a dark turn?

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.040
The teachings of the Jedi Order adhere to
a strict set of philosophies that form a stark

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.140
contrast with those of the Sith.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.320
The Jedi believe emotions dictating actions
can lead to the dark side.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.300
Meanwhile, the Sith embrace the full spectrum
of emotion, good and bad.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.960
And as we've seen, characters like Ahsoka
in the TV shows Clone Wars and Rebels, have

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.160
rejected the Jedi philosophy without actually
going to the dark side.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.370
The Last Jedi heavily teases a darker turn
for Luke Skywalker, but maybe he's not actually

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.760
going to the dark side.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.200
He could certainly reject the Sith's teachings,
too.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:20.160
Either way, the Rogue One debut of the Guardians
of the Whills proves that the Force will still

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:24.260
live on, because it's not always defined by
Jedi Knights and Sith Lords.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.400
The Force will find other guardians, even
if the Skywalker family is finished.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.140
The family name

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.540
The Skywalker saga has been a devastating
one.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.920
Anakin became Darth Vader.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.700
His grandson, Ben Solo, became Kylo Ren.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.800
And now Luke has apparently failed at passing
the way of the Jedi on to the next generation.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.540
For a family with not one but two potential
Chosen Ones, meant to bring balance to the

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.380
Force, that seems like a pretty lousy track
record.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.420
At some point we've got to ask ourselves:
are the Skywalkers doomed?

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:00.020
Yes, the Force and those who use it are always
in a state of flux, in balance one minute

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.190
and out of it the next.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.580
But the Skywalkers in particular seem to have
a more tumultuous relationship with it.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.880
And each Skywalker actually seems to ultimately
doom the next.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.460
Anakin may have saved Luke, but his time as
Darth Vader is what ultimately inspired Ben

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.320
Solo's turn to darkness.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:20.100
And Luke himself failed to teach Ben the ways
of the Jedi, allowing him to be seduced by

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.870
Snoke and the dark side.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.840
If Luke is not, in fact, the Chosen One, and
he has turned away from the light side, the

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.680
Skywalker family may not receive another chance.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.860
Their story, at least as it relates to being
guardians of the Force, may well be over.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:35.760
Unless...

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:37.860
The future of Rey

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:42.840
Rey is a tremendously powerful Force user
and certainly seems to be on the side of good…

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.980
but she still might not take up the traditional
mantle of the Jedi.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.320
While we're being led to believe that Rey
will be a Jedi Master's student, it's becoming

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.880
more clear that may not be the case.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.800
Luke is shown teaching Rey how to command
her powers and how to become more in touch

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.040
with the Force, but that isn't the same thing
as a Jedi Master training a padawan.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.260
Learning to better command the Force won't
automatically make her a Jedi.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.230
With Luke seeming to stray further away from
the traditional teachings of the Jedi, Rey

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.290
could be exposed to elements of the dark side
during her training.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.950
Her journey through the Force will be shaped
by her teacher, and her teacher definitely

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.200
seems to be in a grim place.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.760
That's not to say that Rey will be evil, or
even that her learning more about the dark

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.920
side is a bad thing.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.800
Strictly adhering to a philosophy of pure
good and evil is what led to the fall of the

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.280
Jedi to begin with.

00:04:28.669 --> 00:04:33.020
Rather, it seems likely Rey is going to be
taught not to suppress and control her emotions,

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.040
but to let them guide her when the time is
right.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.960
And they might even guide her to rescuing
Luke himself.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.000
Luke, from the moment he steps on-screen in
The Force Awakens, is clearly in need of help.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:47.340
With Rey's arrival, he's suddenly face-to-face
with a pure-hearted young Force user who could

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.260
restore his faith.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.360
Rey thinks she's here to bring Luke back to
save the galaxy, but the truth may be that

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.410
she's here to save him.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.260
Could she be the key to restoring the Skywalker
legacy for good?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.900
And the Jedi, too?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.060
Thanks for watching!

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.460
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.840
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

